%I A344719 #40 Oct 11 2026 21:56:49
%S A344719 1,2,5,8,11,17,21,28,35,42,51,60,69,80,91,102,115,128,141,156,171,186,
%T A344719 203
%N A344719 Minimum number of cells in an n X n grid that need to be painted so that each unpainted cell is orthogonally adjacent to exactly two painted cells.
%C A344719 From _Shinji Oda_, Oct 04 2026: (Start)
%C A344719 Conjecture: for n >= 6 there is an optimal solution in which every row except the top 2 and bottom 2 rows, ignoring the 2 leftmost and 2 rightmost columns, paints exactly the cells in columns congruent to some s (mod 3). Verified for 6 <= n <= 23.
%C A344719 The optimal solutions found for n = 21, 22, 23 contain a periodic band of 3 rows and 3 columns in the middle. Duplicating this band gives a solution with ceiling((n+2)^2/3) - 6 cells for every larger n in the same residue class mod 3, which together with the values for 7 <= n <= 21 gives the upper bound in the Formula section. (End)
%H A344719 Dmitry Kamenetsky, <a href="/A344719/a344719.txt">Example solutions for n <= 11</a>.
%H A344719 Shinji Oda, <a href="https://github.com/yanyan0207/grid_2fair/tree/v0.3.0">Rust program</a>, 2026.
%H A344719 Puzzling StackExchange, <a href="https://puzzling.stackexchange.com/questions/110250/paint-eleven-squares">Paint Eleven Squares</a>, 2021.
%F A344719 From _Shinji Oda_, Oct 04 2026: (Start)
%F A344719 a(n) <= ceiling((n+2)^2/3) - 6 for n >= 7.
%F A344719 Conjecture: a(n) = ceiling((n+2)^2/3) - 6 for n >= 7.
%F A344719 Conjectured g.f.: x*(1 + 2*x^2 - x^3 + x^5 - 2*x^6 + 3*x^7 - 3*x^8 + 2*x^9 - x^10)/((1-x)^3*(1+x+x^2)). (End)
%Y A344719 Cf. A344301.
